.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-MOUNT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-mount
.Nd mount removable media
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm add | remove Ar device
.Nm
.Cm list
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is called by the hotplug handler when a block device appears or
disappears.
A volume it accepts is mounted at
.Pa /run/media/ Ns Ar label .
It is enabled by
.Va storage.automount
in
.Xr system.conf 5 ,
which
.Nm
reads at event time.
.Bl -tag -width "remove device"
.It Cm add Ar device
Mount it, if it is removable media this system should touch.
.It Cm remove Ar device
Unmount it, lazily, if we mounted it.
For a device still present, use
.Xr novi-eject 1 .
.It Cm list
Removable volumes and their mount points.
.El
.Ss What it refuses, and why most of it is refusing
Every wrong answer here is serious, so most of
.Nm
is deciding whether to touch the device at all.
Removable is two tests rather than one, because a USB hard disk
reports
.Li removable=0 :
the medium is not removable, the device is.
Root, the boot partition, the ESP and the live medium are excluded by
one already-mounted check with no list to keep in sync, and
fstab(5)
is matched on the device node,
.Li LABEL=
and
.Li UUID= ,
because fstab may use any of the three.
.Pp
The filesystem is matched against an
.Sy allowlist ,
never
.Nm mount Fl t Cm auto :
a filesystem driver parsing a hostile image is one of the larger
attack surfaces a kernel has.
Mounts are always
.Cm nosuid,nodev .
.Cm noexec
is deliberately
.Em not
set: it would stop you running a script from a stick, which this
system's own installer does from the live medium, and the attack it
prevents needs the attacker already running code here.
.Ss The label is attacker-controlled
A filesystem label is a string off a stranger's device that is about
to become a directory name.
It is filtered to
.Li [A-Za-z0-9._-] ,
truncated, and a leading dot is
.Sy rejected rather than stripped ,
because
.Pa ..
survives a character filter that keeps dots.
A volume whose label does not survive is mounted under its device
name.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/run/media/<label>" -compact
.It Pa /run/media/ Ns Ar label
Where volumes appear.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-eject 1 ,
.Xr novi-state 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0023.
